{
  "_comment": [
    "Recording from partway into a piece, and the contract both implementations",
    "must keep.",
    "",
    "**Why a fixture rather than a shared function.** The app trims the score to",
    "know where the take's clock starts \u2014 long-rest cues are measured in beats",
    "from the first bar played, so cues computed from bar 1 fire at the wrong",
    "moments for a take that began at bar 12. The backend trims it again before",
    "`build_timeline`, or the analysis compares the recording against bars the",
    "musician never played. Different languages, no way to share the walk, so",
    "this file is the contract \u2014 the same arrangement as `long_rests.json`, and",
    "for the same reason.",
    "",
    "The rules:",
    "",
    "1. Keep every bar from `from_measure` on, with the numbers it has on the",
    "   page. Not rebased to one: a verdict about the fourteenth bar has to say",
    "   fourteen.",
    "2. Drop a repeat that opens before the entry bar, including one that spans",
    "   it \u2014 someone starting mid-passage plays straight on rather than jumping",
    "   back to a sign they never passed.",
    "3. Keep tempo changes at or after the entry bar, plus every one printed",
    "   before it, moved to the entry bar in the order printed. What is in force",
    "   at the entry bar is the point: a `rit.` still running there must not be",
    "   dropped, and a tempo change remembers what it changed from (\"a tempo\"",
    "   after a `rit.` inside a meno mosso returns to the meno mosso), so the",
    "   entry bar is reached through the same markings the page has. The next",
    "   marking in order ends a `rit.`, so one already ended ends again there.",
    "4. A change printed on the entry bar itself supersedes the carried one.",
    "5. Entering at the first bar, or at a bar the piece does not have, changes",
    "   nothing at all.",
    "`stated` (optional) maps a bar number to the metre, clef or key it prints; `out_entry` (optional) is what the first bar of the trimmed score carries."
  ],
